{
  "applications": [
    {
      "description": "Odysseus is a self-hosted personal AI workspace: chat with local or hosted models, run multi-step research over the web, keep a searchable memory of documents and conversations, and receive push notifications when long jobs finish. The install runs four containers on a private loopback network — the Odysseus application itself, a ChromaDB vector store for memory, a SearXNG meta-search engine so web research never goes through a third-party search API, and an ntfy server for notifications. Only the Odysseus web interface and the notification server are published, both to 127.0.0.1 only. Odysseus reaches model servers running on this computer, so it can use XE's own local model server; it also reaches the internet for web search, model downloads and any hosted model API you configure.",
